---
/**
 * @file pages/security.astro
 * @description Security / vulnerability-disclosure policy for akibh.dev and
 *              blog.akibh.dev — the `Policy:` target of both sites'
 *              /.well-known/security.txt (RFC 9116, plan32).
 *
 * WHY THIS CONTENT (POC): a personal site needs only the essentials of a
 * disclosure policy — where to report (email first, socials as a fallback
 * to ask for another channel), what helps, what I promise back, a
 * good-faith safe harbour, what's out of scope (third-party platforms
 * report to their owners), and an honest "no bounty". Scope lists the real
 * moving parts: two static Cloudflare Pages sites, the /api/contact
 * function + the private mailer Worker, the blog's featured-posts API.
 */
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";
import { portfolioData } from "../data/portfolio";

const { meta, socials } = portfolioData;
const updated = "2026-10-23";
const channels = socials.filter((s) => ["GitHub", "LinkedIn", "X"].includes(s.name));
---

<LegalPage
  title="Security"
  description="How to report a security vulnerability in akibh.dev or blog.akibh.dev, what's in scope, and what to expect."
  updated={updated}
>
  <p class="summary">
    <strong>Found a vulnerability?</strong> Thank you — please email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${meta.email}?subject=Security%20report`}>{meta.email}</a> and keep it private until it's fixed.
    I'll reply within 7 days.
  </p>

  <h2>How to report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email (preferred):</strong>{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${meta.email}?subject=Security%20report`}>{meta.email}</a>, with a subject starting with
      "Security".
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Can't use email, or no reply after 7 days?</strong> Message me on{" "}
      {
        channels.map((s, i) => (
          <>
            <a href={s.url}>{s.name}</a>
            {i < channels.length - 2 ? ", " : i === channels.length - 2 ? " or " : ""}
          </>
        ))
      }. Just say you have a security report and we'll agree on a private way to share it — please don't post the
      details there.
    </li>
    <li>
      Please <strong>don't</strong> report vulnerabilities in blog comments, GitHub issues or discussions — they're
      public.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What helps</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The affected URL or component, and what an attacker could do.</li>
    <li>Steps to reproduce (a request, a payload, or a short video), plus browser/tool versions if relevant.</li>
    <li>How you'd like to be credited, if at all.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Scope</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://akibh.dev">akibh.dev</a> — the portfolio, including the contact form (<code>/api/contact</code>) and the mail service behind it.</li>
    <li><a href={meta.blogUrl}>blog.akibh.dev</a> — the blog, including <code>/api/featured</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Out of scope</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party services these sites use — Cloudflare (hosting, Turnstile), GitHub and giscus (comments), Google
      (email). Please report those to their owners.
    </li>
    <li>Denial-of-service, load or spam testing, including flooding the contact form.</li>
    <li>Social engineering or phishing, and physical attacks.</li>
    <li>
      Reports from automated scanners without a demonstrated impact (for example a missing header or a TLS cipher
      note on its own).
    </li>
    <li>My other projects on GitHub — open a private security advisory on that repository instead, or email me.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you can expect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A reply within <strong>7 days</strong>, and updates while I work on it.</li>
    <li>A fix as fast as I can manage, depending on severity — usually within 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      Credit by name or handle once it's fixed, if you'd like it. This is a personal site, so there's
      <strong>no bug bounty</strong>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Good-faith research</h2>
  <p>
    If you act in good faith — test only against these two sites, avoid harming them or their visitors, don't access
    or keep more data than needed to show the problem, stop and tell me if you reach someone else's data, and give me
    a reasonable time to fix it before you publish — I won't take legal action or complain to your provider about
    it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Machine-readable version: <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">/.well-known/security.txt</a>. See also the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> and <a href="/terms/">terms of use</a>.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
